  "worked_solution": "For expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=16$ and $\\phi =\\frac{\\theta }{2}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}^{16} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
